        "name": "Hynne2001_Glycolysis",
        "model_name": "Hynne2001_Glycolysis",
        "sbml_level": 2,
        "sbml_version": 1,
        "notes": "<notes>\n  <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n    <p align=\"right\">The model reproduces Fig 6 of the paper. The stoichiometry and rate of reactions involving uptake of metabolites from extracellular medium have been changed corresponding to Yvol (ratio of extracellular volume to cytosolic volume) mentioned in the publication. The extracellular and cytosolic compartments have been set to 1. Concentration of extracellular glucose, GlcX, is set to 6.7 according to the equation for cellular ",
        "validation_issues": [
          {
            "severity": "info",
            "category": "reversible_formulas",
            "message": "Reversible reaction formulas detected (12 reactions): Glucose Mixed flow to extracellular medium, Glucose uptake, Phosphoglucoisomerase, ... (+9 more)",
            "suggestion": "\u2139\ufe0f  REVERSIBLE REACTIONS WITH SKELLAM DISTRIBUTION:\nReversible reactions with net rate formulas (e.g., k_f*A - k_r*B) are now\nFULLY SUPPORTED in stochastic simulation using the Skellam distribution.\n\nThe \u03c4-leaping engine automatically:\n  \u2713 Detects reversible reaction patterns (formulas with subtraction)\n  \u2713 Uses Skellam sampling: X ~ Poisson(\u03bb_forward) - Poisson(\u03bb_reverse)\n  \u2713 Handles net reverse flux correctly (negative \u0394n values)\n  \u2713 Maintains thermodynamic consistency\n\nSIMULATION MODE RECOMMENDATIONS:\n  \u2713 STOCHASTIC with \u03c4-leaping: Automatically uses Skellam (recommended)\n  \u2713 CONTINUOUS mode: Alternative for very fast reactions\n  \u2713 HYBRID mode: Combines both approaches\n\nReactions with reversible patterns:\n  \u2022 Glucose Mixed flow to extracellular medium: extracellular * k0 * (GlcX0 - GlcX)\n  \u2022 Glucose uptake: (extracellular * V2f / Yvol) * (GlcX / K2Glc / (1 + GlcX / K...\n  \u2022 Phosphoglucoisomerase: cytosol * (V4f * G6P / (K4G6P + G6P + (K4G6P / K4F6P) * F6P)...\n  \u2022 Aldolase: cytosol * (V6f * FBP / (K6FBP + FBP + GAP * K6DHAP * V6f / (...\n  \u2022 Triosephosphate isomerase: cytosol * (V7f * DHAP / (K7DHAP + DHAP + (K7DHAP / K7GAP) * ...\n  ... and 7 more"
          }
        ],
        "layout_type": "compartment_separated",
        "layout_note": "Compartments spatially separated: non-default on periphery, default in center. Use Swiss Palette \u2192 Force-Directed to refine layout."
      }
    },
